-- A ':' with nothing indented under it - every construct that opens a block, left in the state it
-- is in between typing the ':' and typing the first line of the body.
--
-- This is the one recovery that decides whether a file is usable while it is being edited. A block
-- takes its level from its first token, so a block opened on a token that is already at or left of
-- the enclosing level takes the *enclosing* level: every declaration below it is then read as more
-- of the body, and the rest of the file stops existing. Each group here ends with declarations
-- that have to survive.

